From 910de55cf214eac0fe855f98d7100068fa71a1ca Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NeoTech <andreas@roughedge.se>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 22:45:36 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] fix(import): keep STEP items with no unit context in a
 millimetre file

The refusal for an item with no length-unit context also refused files
that state only the millimetre: generated fixtures of bare topology
beside a mm context (import_step_doubly_curved, import_step_thread) and
the corpus row "second copy of the solid" (step_import). The reader
takes 1 mm per unit for such an item, which is the file's own unit, so
the scale is right.

The refusal now applies only when the file states a unit other than the
millimetre (inch, metre, or a mix). The inch pins stay refused.

Pin: millimetre_file_keeps_items_with_no_unit_context.

Refs #2919

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
